WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:01.690
- [Interviewer] All right.

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.050
So are we calling you Lay Low?

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.393
- Yeah, you can call me Lay Low.

00:00:05.393 --> 00:00:06.226
- [Interviewer] Lay Low.

00:00:06.226 --> 00:00:07.960
- [Lay Low] I had several
names at the time,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.783
but Lay Low is one of the names I used,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.333
I had Danno, I had No
Name, and I had Lay Low.

00:00:17.332 --> 00:00:19.850
And the reason I used these names,

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.140
'cause I was selling a dangerous drug

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.350
called fentanyl, right.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.930
When I first brought it down here,

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.063
no one would touch it.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.310
I was living pretty dangerous,

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.900
'cause I was in a school zone,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.130
and I had to change my name several times.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.270
So everything I'm talking about

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.588
I already did time for it,

00:00:37.588 --> 00:00:40.593
so it won't be offending to no one.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.469
So I changed my names a lot of times

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:47.620
so the cops wouldn't know
who they was looking for.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.620
They couldn't put the name with the face,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.810
'cause I had over six blocks.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.410
Nobody would touch fentanyl,

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:54.870
it's a very dangerous drug,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.396
and subsequently everybody
who would touch it,

00:00:58.396 --> 00:01:00.170
and they wasn't familiar with it,

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.628
they probably would die.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.333
Fortunately I didn't get any bodies,

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.210
I made sure I distributed Narcan

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.550
to all the people who use it.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.320
If they got out of prison and came to me,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.413
I would never sell to them.

00:01:15.345 --> 00:01:18.650
The most workers I had was like 15 workers

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.610
at one time,

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.650
I had six blocks,

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:25.220
everybody know me from here to Bakersfield

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.135
to Riverside, my name got pretty big.

00:01:29.135 --> 00:01:32.981
And I was playing cat and
mouse with the cops a lot.

00:01:32.981 --> 00:01:34.940
That's why I changed the name,

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:38.760
Lay Low, Danno, and Lay Low.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.910
So they'd never know who
they was looking for.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.040
Everywhere they go, I'd
be gone to the next spot,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.188
because it's hard to hit a moving target.

00:01:48.188 --> 00:01:52.841
So by me bouncing around
and doing different blocks,

00:01:52.841 --> 00:01:56.760
I was making substantial amount of money.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.663
That went away real fast.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.390
I can say I made over $300,000 downtown

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.500
selling fentanyl.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.332
- [Interviewer] Over what period of time?

00:02:07.332 --> 00:02:10.020
- Less than a year.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.310
I had a nice little run,
about eight, nine months.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.260
I was going through
like, two or three kilos.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.670
I had the cars, you know,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.020
got my mom cars and jewelry and all that,

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.010
but she's the only one that
ended up with everything.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.103
Not me, I ended up basically with nothing.

00:02:28.103 --> 00:02:29.870
It's a hard pill to swallow,

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.262
because when you're used to having

00:02:31.262 --> 00:02:33.540
that kind of money,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.360
and then you go down to basically nothing,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.530
you have to put your pride to the side.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.293
It could destroy you.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.950
- [Interviewer] It was the
conviction that did it.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.040
- Yes, I lost everything.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.860
I was married, wife was gone.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.630
Reconciling with differences,

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.650
she locked up all the money I sent her,

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.260
which that's the only
person I could trust.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.840
'Cause when you make money like that,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.900
you have to trust somebody.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.283
And she kept all the money,
and just divorced me.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.360
They say when you're down,

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.837
sometimes they put dirt on you,

00:03:05.837 --> 00:03:06.830
and that's what happened.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.853
Especially when it come to drug money.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:14.690
I lost relations with my kids behind that,

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:15.670
'cause I wouldn't stop.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:20.670
They liked the money, but it
just wasn't worth it to me.

00:03:20.804 --> 00:03:23.140
The only thing, the highlight of it is,

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.450
I sent my daughter to college.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.700
I was able to get my
oldest daughter Candice

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.533
through college.

00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:31.604
She's graduating next month as we speak,

00:03:31.604 --> 00:03:33.323
she got her doctorate.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.090
And that's a proud moment for me,

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:39.610
for being a drug dealer.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.176
Everybody knows me down here,

00:03:42.176 --> 00:03:44.440
I was pimping and selling drugs,

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.440
and doing all kinds of stuff.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.670
But I was able to get my
daughter through college.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.670
I did something positive with the money.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.960
And she graduates next month,

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.902
she's been in college since she was 17.

00:03:57.902 --> 00:04:00.880
She's 28 now, and for
the most part at first

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.490
I wasn't able to help her.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.100
But I took her to the finish line,

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.830
and I'm a proud dad of that.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:07.863
I don't know what's gonna happen,

00:04:07.863 --> 00:04:09.350
I might not see you next month,

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.650
I might have a heart
attack like Fred Sanford,

00:04:12.579 --> 00:04:13.412
something like that,

00:04:13.412 --> 00:04:14.940
'cause it's a proud moment for me,

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.820
being a dad of five kids.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.670
- [Interviewer] It's great.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.540
So when you were selling,

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.620
you were selling just fentanyl,

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.600
or other drugs too?

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.534
- [Lay Low] I was selling
everything they wanted.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:25.367
- [Interviewer] Everything.

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.860
- [Lay Low] Yeah, from women to ectasy,

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.880
crystal, fentanyl, cocaine, heroin,

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:32.713
whatever you wanted.

00:04:32.713 --> 00:04:34.400
Each block consisted of something.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.233
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:37.034
- [Lay Low] But my money
was in the fentanyl.

00:04:37.034 --> 00:04:40.575
At one point, I was probably
the only one downtown

00:04:40.575 --> 00:04:43.640
you could even get it from.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.753
Five or ten dollars wasn't even an issue.

00:04:45.753 --> 00:04:48.578
You had to have at least
fifty dollars or more

00:04:48.578 --> 00:04:49.700
to purchase that.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.100
It's a very expensive drug.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.506
Now, they buying it for like five dollars.

00:04:53.506 --> 00:04:57.260
So that's another reason I
wouldn't wanna get back in that.

00:04:59.326 --> 00:05:01.940
- [Interviewer] And all of the drugs cut?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.230
- [Lay Low] I had raw fentanyl.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.723
You had to wear a mask,
and if you touched it,

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.240
it could kill you by the smell of it.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.960
You'd have to have a mask,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.090
and when you open it,

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:15.760
fumes go up, and it's just that strong.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.100
It could kill you.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.260
The stuff they getting down
here now is all cut up,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.413
but I had raw fentanyl.

00:05:22.785 --> 00:05:25.060
But like I said, I was
monitoring my situation

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:25.960
very carefully.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:30.593
I didn't get any bodies,
that's the good thing about it.

00:05:30.593 --> 00:05:32.843
- [Interviewer] Do you
tell your customers...

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:41.160
What's your role in the
chain of destruction

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.114
that goes on here?

00:05:42.114 --> 00:05:43.000
(Lay Low chuckles)

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.730
- My role was to go count the money.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.710
Keep up with the money.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:47.705
I had the workers.

00:05:47.705 --> 00:05:51.010
But I always informed
them to give them Narcan,

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.650
pass Narcan out,

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.674
because, Lord forbid, if you get a body,

00:05:54.674 --> 00:05:55.970
you're pretty much done.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.150
I don't think changing your name

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.130
would be able to save you.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.537
'Cause fentanyl, like I said,

00:06:00.537 --> 00:06:03.263
one smell without consuming
it could kill you.

00:06:03.263 --> 00:06:04.096
- [Interviewer] Yeah, that's very...

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:06.070
- So my job was to get the money.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.000
- [Interviewer] But do you
feel any responsibility?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.180
When you put your head
on your pillow at night,

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.570
do you feel any responsibility
in what these people

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.430
are doing to themselves, and all that?

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.280
- Yes, extremely, man.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.800
I had a lot of remorse about doing that.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.593
When I did my time, I
had a lot of long nights.

00:06:21.593 --> 00:06:23.410
Wondering what would happen to this person

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.989
or happen to that person.

00:06:24.989 --> 00:06:27.780
Like I said, that drug
can destroy anybody.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.267
- [Interviewer] Would you
introduce people to fentanyl?

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:32.050
- Never, I would never introduce somebody.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.520
They had to be doing it already,

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.957
and if they just got out of jail,

00:06:35.957 --> 00:06:37.890
they couldn't get none.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.006
And I only allowed people that smoked.

00:06:40.006 --> 00:06:42.010
If I found out you shot fentanyl,

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.650
I would not distribute it.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.327
Nobody that used it intravenously.

00:06:46.327 --> 00:06:49.840
'Cause it's for smoking,
but you can shoot it.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.090
People use it for muscling purposes,

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.790
but the best way to do it is to...

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.337
They say smoking it.

00:06:57.337 --> 00:07:00.373
That's the safest way
to do it, is smoking.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.523
- [Interviewer] How'd you get arrested?

00:07:04.911 --> 00:07:06.740
How'd you get caught?
- Somebody told on me.

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.743
Somebody in my circle told on me.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:15.380
They got a case, and they told
them to give them somebody.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:19.003
And so they did, and I was
getting ready to leave.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.168
If I would have been smart
and left my money in the bank

00:07:23.168 --> 00:07:26.850
instead of drawing it all out
and having a going away party,

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.040
'cause about a year a
half ago I was having

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.300
a going away party,

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.760
and they raided it, and they
got me for over $14,000.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.010
And that was the last of Lay
Low pretty much right there.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:41.940
That was my personal savings that I had,

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.700
and I drawed all the money
out all my bank accounts,

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.830
and I was having a going away party,

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.040
and they raided it.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.340
They raided my house, my tent.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.173
- [Interviewer] Going away?

00:07:52.173 --> 00:07:53.039
Where were you going?

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:55.713
- Up north, Oakland, where my mom is.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.480
I was just gonna go vacation, really,

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.680
but I was ready to quit,
because I had what you call

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:02.943
a tag on me.

00:08:02.943 --> 00:08:06.130
And there were people assigned to me,

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.150
but like I said, by me changing the name,

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.380
they didn't really know who,

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.010
they couldn't put it together as of yet,

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.340
but that's why it's called investigation.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.870
'Cause once they put it together,

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.740
like I said, they tied me.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.320
I never got a direct sale.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:25.030
I was very smart to not to
sell to anyone I did not know.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.743
I didn't take third party money.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.040
If someone that I know that
don't have this kind of money

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.120
bring that money to me, I would bury it

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.010
until later on that night, then I get it.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.600
Because there's such a
thing as marked money.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.360
That's one way they have to get you.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:42.473
They gotta have the money,
the visual, and the drug.

00:08:44.654 --> 00:08:46.570
I'm a critical thinker,

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:49.750
so I was pretty smart not
to let all those elements

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.410
catch up to me at one time.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:56.020
And so when I got ready to go out of town,

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:59.020
they just mysteriously raided the party,

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:04.020
they found drugs, over
$14,000, and gave me

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.653
two years a half in prison.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.780
I did it right there in
Los Angeles County Jail.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.363
The worst time of my life,
the longest time of my life.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.180
But with my influence on the street,

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:19.310
I was able to find a way up out of that.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:22.090
'Cause you get a lot of favor,
and you meet a lot of people.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:26.400
And I'm a people person, so
I buttered a lot of hands,

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.233
and I knew people.

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:29.340
So in there, I got a couple of jobs,

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.580
teacher's aide, went to school,

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.793
and got my time cut off like that.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.689
I had favor everywhere I went.

00:09:36.689 --> 00:09:39.460
Right now, today, people, they know me,

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.593
but I don't know them.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:44.353
Just about anybody
downtown, they know Lay Low.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.462
I put the mark down,

00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:49.426
and I could say I had a
pretty good run with it.

00:09:49.426 --> 00:09:51.723
I had my minute of fame in there.

00:09:52.559 --> 00:09:55.760
I did something nobody else did.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.160
I brought fentanyl down here.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.490
Nobody would touch it,
they were scared of it.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:01.780
I took a chance, and...

00:10:03.809 --> 00:10:07.190
- [Interviewer] What
is... I'm sorry, go ahead.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.390
- I won't say I regret it,

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.723
I just regret the people
that hurt theyself.

00:10:10.723 --> 00:10:13.490
- [Interviewer] What is the
most popular drug currently?

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:14.375
- Right now?

00:10:14.375 --> 00:10:15.208
Fentanyl.

00:10:15.208 --> 00:10:16.041
- [Interviewer] Fentanyl?

00:10:16.041 --> 00:10:16.874
- Yeah.

00:10:16.874 --> 00:10:17.707
- [Interviewer] In the
'80s and '90s it was crack.

00:10:17.707 --> 00:10:19.840
- '80s and '90s it was crack.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.130
I had it running crack, too.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:24.255
I started out selling
drugs when I was like, 15.

00:10:24.255 --> 00:10:28.470
15 to 16, 'cause I had to
buy my own school clothes.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:31.890
So my mom would tell me, "I'm
only gonna give you half.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.070
You gotta get the rest."

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.840
So we had to figure out a way to do it,

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:38.480
and how we did it was
crack cocaine, you know?

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.350
Even in junior high and high school,

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.090
I sold crack cocaine.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:45.420
It went from marijuana to crack to heroin,

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.860
and then when I found
fentanyl, I mastered the game.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.530
Because I did it when I was young,

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:54.960
I just used all my elements
from then into now,

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:59.830
and I just supplied all my
rules to the same thing,

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:02.220
and it worked out just like that.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.530
But eventually you gonna get..

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:05.293
You can't get away with it.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.650
All good comes to an end.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:08.940
- [Interviewer] Everyone
gets caught, right?

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:09.773
- Everyone.

00:11:09.773 --> 00:11:12.253
Nobody gets away, unless...

00:11:12.253 --> 00:11:15.231
Even the people that turn people in,

00:11:15.231 --> 00:11:19.133
they get caught up too, eventually.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.010
Just like they told on somebody,

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.100
somebody else gonna tell on them.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.380
So it's just the same
game played in many ways.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:29.320
And then when you don't do the work,

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:30.781
whatever they want you to do,

00:11:30.781 --> 00:11:32.720
you're like a piece of trash anyway.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:35.313
But one thing about me, I
always just did my time.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.663
No conversation, I would never talk.

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:42.610
- [Interviewer] Did you use it at all?

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:44.733
- Yes, I was my best customer.

00:11:44.733 --> 00:11:47.770
But I had so much, I was
buying a kilo at a time.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.812
- [Interviewer] So you
were using fentanyl?

00:11:49.812 --> 00:11:51.150
- Yeah, I was using fentanyl.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.693
I'd use just about every
kind of drug it is.

00:11:53.693 --> 00:11:55.300
- [Interviewer] Are you using still?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.440
- No, not today.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.297
- [Interviewer] So, how'd
you get off of fentanyl?

00:11:58.297 --> 00:11:59.649
- When I went to prison.

00:11:59.649 --> 00:12:00.482
- [Interviewer] When you went to prison.

00:12:00.482 --> 00:12:01.400
- I had no choice.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.710
But they give you a lot of pills, though.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.660
They give you 10 or 15
pills that'll help you out.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.120
Plus, I suffer from alcoholism,

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.960
and I was addicted to heroin and fentanyl

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.033
all at one time.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:17.159
So when I went there,
they had on the computer

00:12:17.159 --> 00:12:20.020
that I was a chronic user, high tolerance.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.799
So they'd give me like 10 or
15 pills of the best stuff.

00:12:22.799 --> 00:12:23.890
(Lay Low chuckles)

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:28.890
They give me Vicodin,
Klonopins, you name it.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.500
They gave me all the good
stuff, 'cause I needed it.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.290
I was in a lot of pain.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.900
That's the worst kicking drug ever.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.830
It's 10 times stronger
than regular heroin,

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.743
and fentanyl never lost the fight.

00:12:44.168 --> 00:12:46.200
Nobody can beat it.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.033
- [Interviewer] What are the chances

00:12:47.033 --> 00:12:47.993
of you ever using again?

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.560
- Chances of me using it again...

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.760
Probably slim to none.

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:55.733
I'm 52 years old, I'm pretty much tired.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.643
I drink my little liquor, whatever.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.900
Hard drugs is just not for me.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.040
I wanna live the rest of my life peaceful,

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:09.453
see my daughter graduate,
that's all I wanna do.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.453
Fentanyl? Nah.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.640
Too dangerous.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.410
It'll kill you fast.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.243
- [Interviewer] All right.

00:13:17.243 --> 00:13:19.644
Lay Low, thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:13:19.644 --> 00:13:20.783
Very interesting.

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:23.750
- Yeah, that stuff, man...

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:25.903
It's too much.

